  "description": "<p>If you’re looking to pursue higher education or research opportunities in Spain, then enrol at the UCAM Catholic University of Murcia (or Universidad Católica de Murcia). Besides providing academic and individual tutoring, the University fosters teamwork for general development.</p><p>UCAM is also the perfect place to develop your interest in sports. In fact, it's known as the ‘University of Sport’ in Europe and strongly believes that physical activity leads to self-improvement and respect for others.</p><p><strong>About the University</strong></p><p>Founded in 1996, the UCAM Catholic University of Murcia aims at personal and professional success through the transmission of science, technology and culture. It is a private-funded university that maintains 10 faculties. Its approach integrates in-depth theoretical and practical knowledge.&nbsp;</p><p>With a focus on value-based education, the University offers 33 bachelor’s, over 90 master’s and 4 doctoral programs. Additionally, it also provides short online courses like big data fundamentals and application in bioinformatics, leadership and management in an international context, and fundamentals of 3D design and additive manufacturing.</p><p>The UCAM Catholic University of Murcia offers undergraduate and postgraduate courses in business administration, dentistry, modern languages, physical activities and sports sciences, psychology, veterinary medicine, bilingual education, hospitality management, innovation, and tourism marketing. It also provides a Spanish hospitality immersion program.&nbsp;</p><p>Moreover, the University offers master’s degree programs in high-performance sports, management of sports entities, and physical activity and sports sciences.&nbsp;</p><p>At the UCAM Catholic University of Murcia, you can avail of scholarships and grants, including the Fulbright Educational Assistance Program and the European Parliament Fellowship and Internship Program.&nbsp;</p><p>Additionally, the University offers student support services when it comes to curricular and extracurricular internships. Immersive technologies are used in the classroom, and virtual recordings of the classes are available.</p><p><strong>Why choose the UCAM Catholic University of Murcia?</strong></p><p>Here are some reasons:</p><ul><li>Faculty members use the latest technology and related tools for teaching</li><li>The University organises students into small groups so that everyone gets personalised attention</li><li>It ensures well-rounded, high-quality education</li><li>The University has over 2900 international students from 115 nationalities</li></ul>",
